IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law, s 65 — interpretation for Chapter 4 (children's insurance), and the
-- s 1 definition of "ילד" as s 65 reads it. Encoded only as far as ss 66-68 need it.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are generated from line N of the deposited source.
--
-- WHAT THIS SECTION DOES. It defines, for the Chapter, who is "insured" (two limbs) and who
-- is a "child" (two limbs and a proviso), and says when a child out of Israel is not treated
-- as abroad. "Father", "mother" and "parent" follow the definition of "child".
--
-- WHAT IS AN INPUT. Chapter 11 insurance, the s 238 "housewife", residence and the Institute
-- employee's view of an absence, the Administration's authorised person's satisfaction that
-- an insured person supported a child, and the Institute's decision under s 65(b): each is a
-- status or determination that a register records (nii-il06-nouns.l4).

§ `Section 65 — interpretation`
-- src:796 | ⟦ח:קטע2|פרק ד|פרק ד׳: ביטוח ילדים|אחר=[פרק ה׳]⟧
-- src:797 | ⟦ח:קטע3|פרק ד סימן א|סימן א׳: פרשנות⟧
-- src:799 | סעיף 65 – פרשנות [תיקון: תשנ״ז, תשס״ט־4]
-- src:800 | (א) בפרק זה –

§§ `65(a) "insured"`

-- src:801 | ”מבוטח“ –
-- src:802 | (1) מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (1) (source line 802)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "insured" (1) — insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `insured under Chapter 11`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`

-- src:803 | (2) יחיד היושב בישראל, ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר, לדעת עובד המוסד שהוסמך לכך, ואין בו לסתור טענת אותו יחיד כי הוא יושב בישראל, ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2) (source line 803)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "insured" (2) — a resident of Israel not insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `resident in Israel`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `insured under Chapter 11`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח" (source lines 801-803)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — insured` `the person` MEANS
        "(1)" ... `s 65 "insured" (1) — insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person`
    OR  "(2)" ... `s 65 "insured" (2) — a resident of Israel not insured under Chapter 11, other than a housewife` `the person`

-- "one who was insured" (s 65 "ילד" (1)): a person who was insured and, on the day, is not.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — one who was insured` `the person` MEANS
        `the person`'s `formerly insured`
    AND NOT `s 65 — insured` `the person`

§§ `65(a) "child" — whose child`

-- A child's record names its parents; the persons are found by name in the family. After
-- the family's facts are checked (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4) every name resolves to
-- exactly one person; before that, an unresolved name simply finds nobody.
GIVEN `the name`   IS A STRING
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A person`
`the persons named` `the name` `in` `the family` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `name` EQUALS `the name`) (`the family`'s `the persons`)

-- (1) "the child of an insured or of one who was insured", read with s 1, under which
-- "child" includes a stepchild and an adopted child (fork F1): a natural, adoptive or step
-- relation makes the child the person's child.
-- src:170 | ”ילד“ – לרבות ילד חורג וילד מאומץ ולמעט נער ונערה נשואים;
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the entry` IS A `A parent in a child's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the child is the person's child` `the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entry`'s `standing`
    WHEN `the child's natural parent`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child's adoptive parent`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child's step-parent`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who is not the child's parent`   THEN FALSE

-- (2) "one who is not his child, if it is proven, to the satisfaction of whoever the
-- Administration authorised, that in the period set in regulations the insured supported him".
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (2) (source line 806)
GIVEN `the entry`  IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "child" (2) — the insured person named in` `the entry` `supported the child, in` `the family` MEANS
        NOT `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    AND `the entry`'s `support proven`
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured` p) (`the persons named` (`the entry`'s `name of the person`) `in` `the family`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the entry`  IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 "child" (1) — the child of an insured person, or of one who was insured, named in` `the entry` `, in` `the family` MEANS
        `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured` p OR `s 65 — one who was insured` p)
            (`the persons named` (`the entry`'s `name of the person`) `in` `the family`)

-- "the terms 'father', 'mother' and 'parent' shall be construed accordingly": the parents of
-- a child for this Chapter are the persons who make it a child under (1) or (2).
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807)
GIVEN `the entry`  IS A `A parent in a child's record`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a parent for this Chapter, named in` `the entry` `, in` `the family` MEANS
        "(1)" ... `the child is the person's child` `the entry`
    OR  "(2)" ... `s 65 "child" (2) — the insured person named in` `the entry` `supported the child, in` `the family`

-- The parents of the child for this Chapter who are insured on the day: the candidates s 67
-- chooses among. (A person who is "a parent" only under (2) is insured by definition.)
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "מבוטח", "ילד" (source lines 801-807)
GIVEN `the child`  IS A `A child`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
`the insured parents of` `the child` `in` `the family` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD     `s 65 — a parent for this Chapter, named in` e `, in` `the family`
                          AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — insured` p) (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`))
           (`the child`'s `parents`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (1) (source line 805)
GIVEN `the child`  IS A `A child`
      `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`
`the parents of` `the child` `who were insured, in` `the family` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD     `the child is the person's child` e
                          AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `s 65 — one who was insured` p) (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`))
           (`the child`'s `parents`)

§§ `65(a) "child" — the proviso: in Israel, and under 18`

-- "has not reached 18 years": the day is before the 18th anniversary of the birth. For a
-- birth on 29 February the anniversary in a common year is taken as 28 February (`add
-- years` clamps; fork F2).
-- src:807 | ובלבד שהילד נמצא בישראל ולא מלאו לו 18 שנים; והמונחים ”אב“, ”אם“ ו”הורה“ יתפרשו בהתאם לכך.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807)
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` MEANS
    `add years` (`the child`'s `date of birth`) 18

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807)
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `the day` LESS THAN `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child`

§§ `65(b) — a child out of Israel`

-- src:809 | (ב) לא יראו ילד כנמצא בחוץ לארץ אם יצא מישראל לתקופה שאינה עולה על שלושה חודשים; אולם המוסד רשאי לראותו כאילו הוא בישראל גם אם יצא מישראל לתקופה העולה על שלושה חודשים.
-- "left Israel for a period not exceeding three months": the period runs from the day the
-- child left to the day the child returned, or, for an absence not yet ended, to the day
-- asked about (fork F3). Three months from the day of leaving clamps to the end of a shorter
-- month (`add months`; fork F2). "Not exceeding" is inclusive.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809)
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the absence` IS AN `An absence from Israel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence` MEANS
    `the end of the period` AT MOST `add months` (`the absence`'s `the day the child left Israel`) 3
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the absence`'s `the day the child returned to Israel`
            WHEN JUST `the day of return` THEN `the day of return`
            WHEN NOTHING                  THEN `the day`

-- "A child shall not be regarded as abroad if he left Israel for a period not exceeding three
-- months; but the Institute may regard him as if he is in Israel even if he left for a period
-- exceeding three months."
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(b) (source line 809)
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — in Israel on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the child`'s `absence from Israel`
    WHEN NOTHING          THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `the absence` THEN
            "(ב) לא יראו ילד כנמצא בחוץ לארץ" ... `s 65(b) — the absence, as at` `the day` `, is for a period not exceeding three months:` `the absence`
        OR  "אולם המוסד רשאי לראותו כאילו הוא בישראל" ... `the child`'s `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`

§§ `65(a) "child" — the definition`

-- s 1 excludes "a married boy or girl" from "child"; s 65 is read with it (fork F1).
@ref National Insurance Law s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — not a married boy or girl` `the child` MEANS
    NOT `the child`'s `married`

-- Version 0.2.0 (06-S72): asked of a question, the day or the month s 72 pays (nii-il06-nouns.l4,
-- `The question asked of a family on a day`); only the age limb differs between the two (below).
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
      `the child`    IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a child for this Chapter, asked` `the question` `, in` `the family` `:` `the child` MEANS
        (    "(1)" ... any (GIVEN e YIELD `s 65 "child" (1) — the child of an insured person, or of one who was insured, named in` e `, in` `the family`) (`the child`'s `parents`)
         OR  "(2)" ... any (GIVEN e YIELD `s 65 "child" (2) — the insured person named in` e `supported the child, in` `the family`) (`the child`'s `parents`))
    AND "ובלבד שהילד נמצא בישראל" ... `s 65 — in Israel on` (`the family`'s `the day`) `:` `the child`
    AND "ולא מלאו לו 18 שנים"     ... `s 65 — the age limb, asked` `the question` `, on` (`the family`'s `the day`) `:` `the child`
    AND `s 1 — not a married boy or girl` `the child`

-- The day question, as before 0.2.0.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
      `the child`  IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a child for this Chapter, in` `the family` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, asked` `the allowance on the family's day` `, in` `the family` `:` `the child`

§§ `65(a) "child", the proviso's age limb, for a month section 72 pays`

-- Version 0.2.0 (06-S72). s 72(a) pays the allowance from the 1st of the month in which
-- entitlement arose, if it arose by the 15th, and to the last day of the month in which it
-- ceased. So in the month of an 18th birthday the child is paid for although, from the birthday
-- on, it has "reached 18"; and in the month of a birth by the 15th it is paid for although,
-- before the birth, there is no child. s 72 is not encoded in this row (row IL-08 encodes it):
-- which children it pays for in a month is the caller's answer, the children of `A family in a
-- month`. This row reads s 72(a) only to say which of them s 65's age limb lets through for the
-- month: a child whose 18th birthday (as `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` reckons it, fork
-- F2) is on or after the month's first day, and who is born by its last. A listed child outside
-- that is a problem with the facts (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4), not a child left out.
-- src:854 | (א) נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 באותו חודש; נוצרה הזכאות אחרי 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 בחודש שלאחריו; תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות.

@ref National Insurance Law s 72(a) (source line 854): "ב־1 באותו חודש"
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the month of` `the day` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) 1

@ref National Insurance Law s 72(a) (source line 854): "ביום האחרון של החודש"
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the month of` `the day` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (`Days in month` `the day`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807), read with s 72(a) (source line 854)
GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the child` IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child` MEANS
        "תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות" ... `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` `the child` AT LEAST `the first day of the month of` `the day`
    AND "נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני" ...           `the child`'s `date of birth` AT MOST `the last day of the month of` `the day`

-- The age limb, for the question asked: under 18 on the day; or, for the month s 72 pays, not 18
-- before the month began and born by its end.
@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד", proviso (source line 807); s 72(a) (source line 854)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the day`      IS A DATE
      `the child`    IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — the age limb, asked` `the question` `, on` `the day` `:` `the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `the allowance on the family's day`
    THEN `s 65 — under 18 on` `the day` `:` `the child`
    WHEN `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
    THEN `s 65, read with s 72(a) — not 18 before the month of` `the day` `began, and born by its end:` `the child`

§§ `A family in a month, as a family on its day`

-- `A family in a month` (nii-il06-nouns.l4) put as a family on the day its facts stand on, its
-- children being the ones s 72 pays for in the month. Every rule of ss 65-68 that takes a family on
-- a day answers the month when asked `the allowance for the month of the family's day, …`.
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family in a month`
GIVETH A `A family on a day`
`the family in a month, on its day:` `the family` MEANS
    `A family on a day` WITH
        `the day`        IS `the family`'s `a day in the month, on which the facts stand`
        `the persons`    IS `the family`'s `the persons`
        `the children`   IS `the family`'s `the children section 72 pays for in the month`

@ref National Insurance Law s 65(a) "ילד" (source lines 804-807), s 1 "ילד" (source line 170), s 72(a) (source line 854)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family in a month`
      `the child`  IS A `A child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65 — a child for this Chapter, for the month section 72 pays, in` `the family` `:` `the child` MEANS
    `s 65 — a child for this Chapter, asked` `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
        `, in` (`the family in a month, on its day:` `the family`) `:` `the child`
